	"name": "Angelic Jelly",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-splashing-yellow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>These Tiny yellow oozes resemble golden, semi-transparent bats or birds and emit a faint glow as they glide along wind currents. While they are amorphous like all oozes, angelic jellies spend their entire lives in flight, and every flap of their pseudo- wings produces a faint, chime-like sound. A DC 14 Religion check reveals that angelic jellies are only found in places of profound holy significance, just as hallowed ground or areas blessed by the gods.</p>",
